	)
	(text
		"J1 JST XH S2B-XH-A: pin1 VIN_12V_RAW, pin2 GND. Mate with XHP-2 housing.  Pin 1 is the +12 V pin."
		(at 17.28 121.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "49b26855-027b-5483-9368-23594b1558a8")
	)
	(text
		"F1 1.5 A hold PPTC, then Q1 AO3401A P-FET (30 V Vds, 12 V Vgs max, 4 A) reverse-polarity switch (body diode to start, Vgs clamped to -5.1 V by D_QG)."
		(at 17.28 123.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7868e459-381d-50cb-be7d-53d1d061887d")
	)
	(text
		"Q1 gate check: the 5.1 V zener D_QG across source and gate limits Vgs to about 5.1 V, within the AO3401A 12 V gate-source rating. The drain sees at most the TVS clamp of 21.5 V (D_TVS is upstream of Q1), below the AO3401A 30 V drain-source rating by 8.5 V."
		(at 17.28 126.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b7c95048-3308-5410-a6d5-806937c51b4d")
	)
	(text
		"D_TVS SMAJ13A (Littelfuse, 400 W, VR 13.0 V, VBR 14.40 to 15.90 V at 1 mA, IR 1 uA maximum at VR, VC 21.5 V at IPP 18.6 A) sits on VIN_FUSED, before Q1: its cathode joins the fused input net on the Q1 drain side and its anode is on GND, so a surge is clamped before it reaches Q1, the buck or any capacitor. A reversed supply forward-biases D_TVS, which conducts and opens F1; Q1 then isolates the protected rail."
		(at 17.28 128.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "aed6ecbf-4f7d-54f3-b2a2-340c5d78d0cf")
	)
	(text
		"TVS check: the supply maximum is 13.0 V, equal to the 13.0 V standoff VR, so leakage at the maximum input is the datasheet IR of 1 uA maximum, and 13.0 V is 1.4 V below the 14.40 V minimum breakdown. Worst-case clamp 21.5 V is below the MP2307 recommended input maximum 23 V by 1.5 V and its absolute maximum 26 V by 4.5 V, below the AO3401A 30 V Vds by 8.5 V, and below the 25 V rating of C_BULK, C_IN1, C_IN2 and C_N7 by 3.5 V."
		(at 17.28 131.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "debe7c3c-5035-5d31-a37f-60f3629d6ef8")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 19.21 399.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "51bbc1e5-3d27-5647-a800-3f9f245491e2")
	)
	(text
		"MP2307 (internal sync rectifier, 340 kHz). Vout = 0.925 V x (1 + 26.1k/10k) = 3.34 V."
		(at 19.21 403.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "95489d0b-8d55-50b6-b06f-6b50ad1738de")
	)
	(text
		"L1 10 uH: ripple about 0.7 A p-p at 12 V in; confirm L1 saturation current against its datasheet."
		(at 19.21 406.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "63aeac58-1ed2-5caa-84df-3d9c6501978f")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 211.9 380.825 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "204678eb-4dd1-5635-b988-2dd7fe54aa64")
	)
	(text
		"J_SWD pin1 +3V3, pin2 SWDIO, pin3 GND, pin4 SWCLK, pin5 NRST. No USB bootloader; program over SWD."
		(at 211.9 384.825 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3a71104c-06df-58ab-9ae3-a73c6acdf46b")
	)
	(text
		"HSE 8 MHz on PC14/PC15 (OSC_IN/OSC_OUT). Crystal NDK NX3225GD-8MHZ-STD-CRA-3, CL 8 pF. CL = (C1 x C2)/(C1 + C2) + Cstray with Cstray 5 pF, so C1 = C2 = 2 x (8 - 5) = 6 pF. Nearest standard value (E24) 6.2 pF: CL = 6.2/2 + 5 = 8.1 pF, 0.1 pF from 8 pF (limit 0.5 pF). Cstray 5 pF is an assumption, not measured."
		(at 211.9 387.365 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8960bdf2-5f38-576a-b856-f16c7fd2208c")
	)
	(text
		"Boot: PA14 (SWCLK) is BOOT0; default option bytes boot from flash."
		(at 211.9 389.905 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "13d0fa0b-e69f-5f60-ae7b-acfdc6b9db0c")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 212.08 496.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7119d35f-4f8b-5564-89a3-bca284fd7a77")
	)
	(text
		"J_VALVE1 pin1 +12V_VALVE, pin2 VALVE1_SW (low-side). Flyback cathode to +12V_VALVE."
		(at 212.08 500.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7298a15b-922e-565c-b735-2a3aac2975ad")
	)
	(text
		"Load: 12 V DC solenoid, coil current at most 0.5 A. AO3400A carries 0.5 A (rated far above, needs datasheet value sourcing for the exact figure), flyback diode 1N5819-class (1 A class), VALVE1_SW is class PWR12 (0.8 mm, about 8x the width a 0.5 A / 10 C rise needs)."
		(at 212.08 503 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "565c3cc7-77d3-5804-ae62-08b6377a5d61")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 544.92 140.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7d11b848-25dd-5c74-85df-9202f16cde6d")
	)
	(text
		"J_VALVE2 pin1 +12V_VALVE, pin2 VALVE2_SW (low-side). Flyback cathode to +12V_VALVE."
		(at 544.92 144.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "41959647-8a57-5213-b415-536d900765b5")
	)
	(text
		"Load: 12 V DC solenoid, coil current at most 0.5 A. Same checks as valve 1: MOSFET, flyback diode and PWR12 tracks carry 0.5 A."
		(at 544.92 147.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b8423335-6223-537c-b17d-3ce33258f744")
	)
	(text
		"R_SN2 100 ohm in series with C_SN2 10 nF is an RC snubber across the valve 2 coil connector. TP_V2 probes VALVE2_SW. C_B3 100 nF bypasses +12V_VALVE beside the valve 2 driver; R_B3 47 k bleeds the 12 V rail: 13.0 V / 47 k = 0.277 mA, 3.6 mW."
		(at 544.92 149.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d93b842e-5ef9-59c9-af3a-6d63605c0add")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 797.65 166.195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1d921918-7fba-510d-98f9-4d781a6debb9")
	)
	(text
		"J_SOIL1 pin1 excitation, pin2 sense, pin3 GND. Probe between pins 1 and 2. Excitation off by default (gate pulled to +3V3)."
		(at 797.65 170.195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "29a7c69e-dd2d-596c-ab9c-bc9653c413d5")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 990.69 166.195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c3301358-11fd-53d3-a720-3762844bf4be")
	)
	(text
		"J_SOIL2 pin1 excitation, pin2 sense, pin3 GND. Probe between pins 1 and 2. Excitation off by default (gate pulled to +3V3)."
		(at 990.69 170.195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f5b1091a-15d5-5ea4-b8bc-342f1bf3028f")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 544.99 317.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "469dd56d-d6bd-51b3-a15f-4b2713a14b0d")
	)
	(text
		"J_FLOW pin1 +12V_VALVE sensor supply, pin2 GND, pin3 pulse. Open-collector assumed; 3.3 V zener D_FZ (cathode on FLOW_PULSE, anode on GND) behind R_FS 2.2 k clamps a push-pull output to the STM32G030 input range. Current at a 13.0 V sensor output: (13.0 - 3.3) / 2.2 k = 4.41 mA (12 V: 3.95 mA), about 3.3 V x 4.41 mA = 14.5 mW in the zener, far below a 500 mW SOD-123 zener class rating (exact rating needs datasheet sourcing). With the line open the 10 k pull-up R_FPU on +3V3 holds it at 3.3 V, so R_FPU adds at most 3.3 V / 10 k = 0.33 mA."
		(at 544.99 321.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "3b21b531-5a31-5f60-bf5c-41037b5e391c")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 544.78 478.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a6039bc5-0e1a-556d-950a-e3746d012e58")
	)
	(text
		"Addresses: APDS-9301 0x29 (ADR_SEL low), 24LC256 0x50 (A2..A0 low). No collisions. An SHT30 breakout attaches to J_I2C at address 0x44, which stays free; the on-board SHT30 was removed because its 0.5 mm DFN cannot be escaped on two layers."
		(at 544.78 482.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7fec04c3-3ce2-5493-bfa9-f2365eeae2cd")
	)
	(text
		"J_I2C pin1 GND, pin2 +3V3, pin3 SDA, pin4 SCL. 3.3 V only, no 5 V; external load <= 100 mA."
		(at 544.78 485.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ad8d548d-5a45-5ebb-bf6b-5a45602c7019")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 17.91 643.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "564777df-7a6b-524c-81c2-a50abca8a3fd")
	)
	(text
		"D_PWR lit when +3V3 is present. D_VALVE lit when firmware commands either valve on."
		(at 17.91 647.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "85d5ff23-7967-518e-a6e0-fd4006ff394c")
	)
	(text
		"D_N1 lit when +12V_VALVE is present (R_N3), D_N2 lit when +3V3 is present (R_N4)."
		(at 17.91 650.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1e9abaf9-2b8b-5872-a390-bd5a0d956fe6")
	)
	(text
		"LED currents are I = (V - Vf) / R; the Vf of the selected LEDs is not yet read from their datasheets (needs sourcing), so the upper bound with Vf = 0 is given and the real current is lower. D_PWR, R_PWR 680: at most 3.3 V / 680 = 4.85 mA. D_VALVE, R_LV 680, driven from MCU pin PA7 at 3.3 V: at most 4.85 mA, which the pin must source (needs the STM32G030 pin current limit sourced). D_N2, R_N4 680 on +3V3: at most 4.85 mA. D_N1, R_N3 2.2 k on +12V_VALVE: at most 13.0 V / 2.2 k = 5.9 mA at 13.0 V, 12 V / 2.2 k = 5.5 mA nominal, about 77 mW in R_N3 at 13.0 V, within a 0603 resistor rating only if that rating is confirmed (needs sourcing)."
		(at 17.91 652.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "420efc78-5ffc-527e-ab84-7cffdefc9234")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 737.44 613.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6ea0d053-4888-5e28-b5e7-80026eec5769")
	)
	(text
		"+3V3 bulk and high-frequency decoupling; R_N1 and R_N2 are bleeders across +3V3."
		(at 737.44 617.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b9c66e1e-291a-5596-9ba9-5c1ebf00e41f")
	)
	(text
		"C_B8 4.7 uF adds bulk decoupling to +3V3 beside the MCU. C_B2 and C_B4 100 nF plus C_B5 4.7 uF add high-frequency and bulk decoupling to +3V3 near the I2C parts. R_B2 100 k and R_B4 47 k are bleeders across +3V3 (3.3 V / 100 k = 33 uA and 3.3 V / 47 k = 70 uA); R_N1 100 k and R_N2 47 k give the same 33 uA and 70 uA, so the four bleeders draw 206 uA in total, 0.68 mW. TP_SDA and TP_SCL probe the I2C bus."
		(at 737.44 619.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9fd010f5-8bdc-598e-bd5d-810701b5c3bd")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 17.56 783.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2334b112-942a-5789-bd0f-3c5e9b4d048e")
	)
	(text
		"+12V_VALVE decoupling and bleeders."
		(at 17.56 787.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b3449cc9-c803-5505-a0d7-f0a7a77f69f5")
	)
	(text
		"R_B1 bleeds C_BULK (100 k, 13.0 V / 100 k = 0.130 mA). R_N5 and R_N6 are 100 k bleeders on the same rail, 0.130 mA each. Resistive bleed of the +12V_VALVE rail: R_N5, R_N6, R_B1 (100 k each) and R_B3 (47 k) in parallel are 19.5 k, 0.67 mA at 13.0 V; with R_EN 100 k to the buck enable 16.3 k. C_BULK 100 uF plus about 30 uF of other capacitance on the rail (C_IN1, C_IN2 10 uF each, C_N7 10 uF, small 100 nF parts) is about 130 uF, so the time constant is 16.3 k x 130 uF = 2.1 s and the rail is below 5 % (3 tau) in about 6 s, ignoring the faster discharge through the buck, LED and valve loads. C_B1 is 100 nF high-frequency bypass on +12V_VALVE. R_SN1 100 ohm in series with C_SN1 10 nF is an RC snubber across the valve 1 coil connector. TP_V1 is a test point on VALVE1_SW."
		(at 17.56 790.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4490a645-0515-5b8f-942e-f8f96b1de3c5")
	)
	(text
		""
		(at 1080.69 751.73 0)
